    "body": "Cause, reproduced in a worktree from `origin/main` (`e3ca44fa7`), debug, `cargo xtask gate test the_committed_project_posts_the_committed_program --crate camcraft-app --binary first_4axis_part --exact`:\n\n```\nthe machine check: \"Flat A-90: inputs moved since generation - regenerate before posting\"\n```\n\nThe test stops at the machine check. It does not get to the compare of the posted program. The output of the post did not change: `the_first_4axis_part_posts_its_indexed_program` builds the same job through the commands, posts it, and is still equal to `examples/first-4axis-part.nc`.\n\nThe red start is earlier than the merges named in the issue body:\n\n- Post-merge run 43870387249 on `4b7a6b1e8` is also red with this test. The last green run is on `ef1f53451`.\n- A local run on `4b7a6b1e8` fails with the same message.\n- PR #2155 (#2152, merged in `f90e9dc8e`) changed the stamp salt in `crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs` from `camcraft-op-stamp-v2` to `camcraft-op-stamp-v3`. The intent: each cache from before reads stale one time, and the post refuses it until a regenerate.\n- PR #2135 (merged in `abfe679e2`) added `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj`. Its branch did not contain `f90e9dc8e`, thus the committed project holds v2 stamps.\n- The two PRs were never tested together. The merges #2167 to #2087 are not the cause.\n\nReading: the refusal is the correct output. A cache with an old stamp must not post. The committed example project is stale. The fix regenerates the project with the documented command `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_4axis_part`. No code changes.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
